    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening leadership</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The John Allwright Fellowship (JAF) allows scientists from partner countries involved in ACIAR research projects to obtain postgraduate qualifications at an Australian tertiary institution. The program offers PhD and master&apos;s by research scholarships to agricultural researchers, administered through the Australia Awards system.
&#x200d;
As part of ongoing ACIAR-funded efforts to restore damaged coral reefs led by Southern Cross University (SCU), local Filipino researcher Dr Dexter Dela Cruz was selected to complete a JAF, graduating from SCU with a PhD in Marine Biology in 2019. 
&#x200d;
Dr Dela Cruz has continued to be instrumental in ACIAR-supported reef restoration projects. These projects have achieved worldwide recognition for developing techniques to raise coral larvae in aquaculture facilities before releasing them into the sea. Now recognised internationally as a leading coral researcher, Dr Dela Cruz was named the Alumnus of the Year by the Australian Embassy in the Philippines for the 2024 Australia Alumni Excellence Awards.</narrative>
    </description>
